    <section>
      <h2>How Karst works</h2>
      <ol class="steps" id="tutorial"><li><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label"><span class="gs-step-label">Set up with agent</span></div><div class="step-desc">Use the manifest row in the setup checklist above.</div></div></li><li><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label"><span class="gs-step-label">Create your first ticket</span></div><div class="step-desc">Describe the work; Karst fetches or drafts the context brief.</div><button type="button" class="k-btn k-btn--sm step-action k-btn--secondary" title="Open the create-ticket panel">Create ticket</button></div></li><li><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label"><span class="gs-step-label">Pick repos + approach and launch the session</span></div><div class="step-desc">Choose the repositories and the approach, then start the session</div></div></li><li><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label"><span class="gs-step-label">Watch stage progress on the ticket dashboard</span></div><div class="step-desc">Follow the ticket through its stages on the ticket dashboard.</div></div></li><li><div class="step-body"><div class="step-label"><span class="gs-step-label">Optional: install an approach package</span></div><div class="step-desc">Add a curated method (agents, commands, skills) from Settings → Approaches.</div><button type="button" class="k-btn k-btn--sm step-action k-btn--secondary" title="Open the Karst settings panel">Open settings</button></div></li></ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Report an issue</h2>
      <p class="section-desc">
        Use this when Karst itself fails, for example a stuck stage or a blank panel.
        You review the redacted report before it leaves your machine.
      </p>
      <details class="section-desc">
        <summary>What the report contains</summary>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Karst collects its own diagnostics (runtime versions, stage and gate state, effective
          configuration, bounded logs) and redacts secrets, paths and credentials. Approve the report
          and Karst hands the redacted summary to a prefilled GitHub issue in your browser. You still
          press Submit there. Ticket descriptions and other prompt text are left out unless you opt in
          during the review step. For work items in your own project, create a ticket instead.
        </p>
      </details>
      <div class="toolbar">
        <button type="button" class="k-btn k-btn--secondary" id="report-issue" title="Collect redacted Karst diagnostics and open a prefilled GitHub issue">Report an issue</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <button type="button" class="k-btn k-btn--ghost" id="dismiss">Do not open at start-up</button>
    </footer>

